<!--
  TipTapReadyDemo.rozie — behavioral cell for TipTap's `ready` event (quick 260925-r41).

  Reported from dogfooding (oinbox): a consumer can't tell when focusEditor() will work,
  so it waited two animation frames and focused the [contenteditable] by hand. `ready`
  fires once the editor exists, with the live Editor as its payload.

  Two editors, one per construction path:
    - `plain` uses no conditional feature, so it is constructed synchronously at mount;
    - `counted` sets maxLength, so its CharacterCount extension is loaded with a dynamic
      import() first and the editor is constructed a tick later.
  Each records its ready payload; `counted` focuses its editor FROM the handler — the exact
  consumer need — through the payload, not a component ref (Angular's ref is the host).

  Audit follow-up (quick 260926): `plain-ready-count` / `counted-ready-count` tally EVERY
  `ready` fire (not just the latest status) — tiptap-strictmode.spec.ts asserts
  `counted-ready-count` stays "1" through a React-StrictMode dev-mode double-invoke,
  proving only the live invocation's async construction path actually constructs.

  Also (quick 260926): `counted` now wires `@error`, recording the extension name from
  the event payload. tiptap-import-failure.spec.ts aborts the CharacterCount chunk's
  network request and asserts BOTH that `error` fires with `{ extension: 'count', error }`
  AND that the editor still constructs WITHOUT that extension (degrade, not a permanently
  uncreated editor) — see TipTap.rozie's $onMount comment for the fix.

  Autofocus-timing cell (quick 260927-a2u): a THIRD editor, `auto`, sets the declarative
  `:autofocus="true"` prop and does NOT call any focus command itself — the whole point is
  observing TipTap's OWN autofocus, unlike `counted`, which proves the IMPERATIVE path
  (`editor.commands.focus('end')` called directly from its `ready` handler, bypassing
  TipTap's autofocus machinery entirely).

  Two DISTINCT signals are recorded, and this split is load-bearing — a global
  `document.activeElement` poll (the first thing tried) CANNOT prove this reliably, for a
  reason discovered only by measuring with instrumented `requestAnimationFrame`/`.focus()`
  patches (`page.addInitScript`, one animation frame, ~40ms after navigation, on both
  react and vue): TipTap's `focus` command (`@tiptap/core` `src/commands/focus.ts`) ITSELF
  defers the actual `view.focus()` DOM call through `requestAnimationFrame` inside
  `delayedFocus()` — a SECOND deferral layered on top of `Editor.mount()`'s own
  `window.setTimeout(fn, 0)` that schedules the declarative `autofocus` command in the
  first place. Measured: `auto`'s autofocus DOES call `.focus()` on its own contenteditable
  (its `mount()` macrotask fires first, since `auto` needs no lazy extension) — but
  `counted`'s handler-triggered `editor.commands.focus('end')` (fired a few ms later, once
  its CharacterCount dynamic import() settles) schedules its OWN `requestAnimationFrame`
  that lands in the SAME animation frame, and rAF callbacks run in scheduling order — so
  `counted`'s later-scheduled callback fires SECOND within that frame and steals final
  document focus back, sub-millisecond after `auto` transiently held it. No
  `expect.poll` (100ms-scale sampling) can ever observe that transient state — which is
  why the two signals below are event-driven, not poll-driven:
    - `autoFocusedSync` — read `editor.isFocused` SYNCHRONOUSLY inside `onAutoReady`,
      the instant `ready` fires. Always `false`: proves `ready` fires strictly BEFORE
      the deferred `setTimeout(0)` autofocus command has run at all (the plan's core
      claim — confirmed, not just plausible).
    - `autoFocusedEver` — set by a `@focus` listener (TipTap's own pre-existing `focus`
      event, `onFocus: () => $emit('focus')` in TipTap.rozie) the first time the `auto`
      editor's contenteditable genuinely receives DOM focus. Event listeners can't miss a
      transient state the way a poll can, so this reliably proves autofocus DID engage —
      even though, per the mechanism above, `counted` immediately reclaims final page
      focus and `auto`'s OWN contenteditable does not end up holding document focus by
      the time a test can observe it.
  Net finding for the todo: `ready` becoming `'ready'` does not mean declarative
  `autofocus` has landed — it fires strictly before the FIRST of two deferral layers even
  runs — and the reverse question ("does it eventually land?") has a strictly weaker
  answer than expected: autofocus DOES fire, but only transiently, and is not guaranteed
  to still hold document focus even one frame later if any other editor on the page also
  requests focus around the same time (this demo's own `counted` cell reliably does).
-->

<rozie name="TipTapReadyDemo">

<components>
{
  TipTap: '../../packages/ui/tiptap/src/TipTap.rozie',
}
</components>

<data>
{
  plainHtml: '<p>Plain</p>',
  countedHtml: '<p>Counted</p>',
  autoHtml: '<p>Auto</p>',
  plainReady: 'waiting',
  countedReady: 'waiting',
  autoReady: 'waiting',
  plainReadyCount: 0,
  countedReadyCount: 0,
  autoReadyCount: 0,
  countedError: '(none)',
  autoFocusedSync: 'unknown',
  autoFocusedEver: 'no',
}
</data>

<script>
const onPlainReady = (editor) => {
  $data.plainReady = editor && typeof editor.getHTML === 'function' ? 'ready' : 'no editor'
  $data.plainReadyCount = $data.plainReadyCount + 1
}
const onCountedReady = (editor) => {
  if (!editor || typeof editor.getHTML !== 'function') {
    $data.countedReady = 'no editor'
    $data.countedReadyCount = $data.countedReadyCount + 1
    return
  }
  editor.commands.focus('end')
  $data.countedReady = 'ready'
  $data.countedReadyCount = $data.countedReadyCount + 1
}
const onCountedError = (payload) => {
  $data.countedError = payload && payload.extension ? payload.extension : 'error-no-context'
}
// Deliberately does NOT call any focus command — this cell observes TipTap's OWN
// declarative `autofocus` prop, not an imperative override of it (see header comment).
const onAutoReady = (editor) => {
  if (!editor || typeof editor.getHTML !== 'function') {
    $data.autoReady = 'no editor'
    $data.autoReadyCount = $data.autoReadyCount + 1
    return
  }
  // Read SYNCHRONOUSLY, in the same tick `ready` fires — before TipTap's own deferred
  // `setTimeout(0)` autofocus command (Editor.mount()) has had a chance to run. Expected
  // 'no' — see header comment for the measured mechanism.
  $data.autoFocusedSync = editor.isFocused ? 'yes' : 'no'
  $data.autoReady = 'ready'
  $data.autoReadyCount = $data.autoReadyCount + 1
}
// TipTap's own pre-existing `focus` event (onFocus: () => $emit('focus')) — fires the
// moment the `auto` editor's contenteditable genuinely receives DOM focus, regardless of
// whether that focus is later reclaimed by another editor on the page (see header comment).
const onAutoFocus = () => {
  $data.autoFocusedEver = 'yes'
}
</script>

<template>
<div class="tiptap-ready-demo">
  <div data-testid="plain"><TipTap r-model:html="$data.plainHtml" @ready="onPlainReady" /></div>
  <div data-testid="counted"><TipTap r-model:html="$data.countedHtml" :maxLength="50" @ready="onCountedReady" @error="onCountedError" /></div>
  <div data-testid="auto"><TipTap r-model:html="$data.autoHtml" :autofocus="true" @ready="onAutoReady" @focus="onAutoFocus" /></div>
  <pre data-testid="plain-ready">{{ $data.plainReady }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="counted-ready">{{ $data.countedReady }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="auto-ready">{{ $data.autoReady }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="plain-ready-count">{{ $data.plainReadyCount }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="counted-ready-count">{{ $data.countedReadyCount }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="auto-ready-count">{{ $data.autoReadyCount }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="counted-error">{{ $data.countedError }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="auto-focused-sync">{{ $data.autoFocusedSync }}</pre>
  <pre data-testid="auto-focused-ever">{{ $data.autoFocusedEver }}</pre>
</div>
</template>

<style>
.tiptap-ready-demo {
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  color: #1a1a1a;
  padding: 1rem;
  max-width: 720px;
}
</style>

</rozie>
